{"title":"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A train stops at Waterloo Station every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes. A bus stops at Waterloo Station every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes. A train and a bus both stop at Waterloo Station at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3f30ec07df73171e4885bc61483935a089ffacd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6:25 \\text{ a.m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" />. The next time that a train and a bus both stop at Waterloo Station at the same time is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/f/88fd2c3f58eb4741e88c367fe42bc9f39193edaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 6:28 \\text{ a.m.} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 6:30 \\text{ a.m.} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 6:33 \\text{ a.m.} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 6:40 \\text{ a.m.} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 6:55 \\text{ a.m.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"702\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The least common multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/d/6dda8115d8d4a649a1736b3797df21af5fbb54fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 3 = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> because both numbers are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Relatively_prime\" title=\"Relatively prime\">relatively prime</a> (have a greatest common divisor/GCD of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), so both will stop at Waterloo Station again after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes.\n</p><p>Since they both stopped at the same time at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2c934b1960f153b676bd33ca49fe309cff51d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6:25 \\text{ a.m.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />, the next time this would happen would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a3406694b9bead361cfecd19004136c2533924d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(D) } 6:40 \\text{ a.m.}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"128\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><